DOS-PORT (patch 0103, Phase 10 Stage 4). Concrete OPL3 (YMF262) FM
synthesis MidiBackend implementation routing MIDI events to the
SB16/Vibra16S-built-in OPL3 chip via SDL/0037+'s OPL3 helpers
(SDL_DOSOpl3* family). 18 x 2-op voice allocator with round-robin
LRU steal; small inline GM patch bank covering 7 family categories;
per-MIDI-channel program / volume / expression state.

Selected when SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_BACKEND=opl3. SoundManager::init()
probes via SDL_DOSOpl3Detect (Adlib timer-1 sequence per AdLib spec);
on success, calls SDL_DOSOpl3InitChip (enables 18x2-op mode, silences
all voices) + installs MidiBackendOpl3 on the singleton MidiScheduler.
On probe failure: same graceful-degradation pattern as Stage 3's
MidiBackendWaveBlaster -- engine rolls active backend back to organya
with clear LOG_INFO; Pixtone SFX continues unchanged on SB16 DAC.

NEW files (2):

  src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.{h,cpp} -- MidiBackendOpl3 class:
    Constructor: probe + InitChip + arm voice allocator + reset per-
      MIDI-channel state to GM defaults (program=0 Acoustic Grand
      Piano; volume=100 medium-loud; expression=127 full-on).
    Voice allocator: 18 x 2-op layout per design sec. D.5;
      _allocate_voice() prefers free voices (lowest-ID for
      determinism); LRU-steals when all 18 are busy. Tracks per-voice
      (active, midi_channel, midi_note, last_used).
    note_on: allocate voice + apply patch (drum patch on channel 9;
      family-bucket patch otherwise) + convert MIDI note -> OPL3
      (fnum, block) via 12-entry octave-base lookup table + trigger
      key-on.
    note_off: reverse-lookup voice for (channel, note) + clear key-on;
      idempotent silent no-op when no match (handles redundant note-
      offs from SMF arrangements).
    control_change: handles CC 7 (volume), CC 11 (expression), CC 120
      (All Sound Off), CC 123 (All Notes Off); other CCs ignored
      (slot 0103 placeholder; Phase 10.5 may add more).
    program_change: updates per-channel current GM program;
      subsequent notes pick up the new patch (per GM spec -- held
      notes keep original patch).
    on_song_start / on_song_stop: silence all voices + reset per-
      channel state to GM defaults.
    Destructor: silence all + SDL_DOSOpl3Shutdown (idempotent).

    Inline patch bank (8 patches): PATCH_PIANO, PATCH_MALLET,
    PATCH_ORGAN, PATCH_GUITAR, PATCH_BRASS, PATCH_REED, PATCH_PAD,
    PATCH_DRUM. 12 bytes each per the SDL_DOSOpl3VoiceWritePatch
    contract (op0[0..4] + channel FB/CONN [5] + op1[6..10] +
    fine-tune [11]). Programs 0-127 collapse into 16 GM family
    buckets which map to one of the 7 melodic patches; channel 9
    uses PATCH_DRUM ignoring program field.

  Sourcing: patches transcribed from publicly-documented OPL3
  register conventions in the AdLib SBI (Sound Bank Instrument)
  format documentation (AdLib Inc. 1991 OPL2 programmer's manual
  + Yamaha YMF262 datasheet) + reference patches in the Apogee Sound
  System documentation that Apogee/3D Realms released as open-source
  GPLv2 with the 1997 DOOM/Heretic/RotT source-release series.

  Aesthetic disclosure: this 8-patch placeholder will sound generic-
  FM on real OPL3. Phase 10.5 follow-up may swap in a fuller
  community bank (e.g., libADLMIDI's wohlstand_default OPL3 bank ~
  175 patches MIT-licensed) via runtime data/opl3-patches.dat
  loader when operator listening identifies tracks needing better
  timbre. THIRD-PARTY.md backlog tracks attribution for whichever
  full bank gets adopted.

