+/* Cave Story port -- Phase 10 Stage 4 (slot 0103). MidiBackendOpl3
+ * implementation. See MidiBackendOpl3.h for design + API contract.
+ *
+ * Patch bank sourcing -- community attribution (per team-lead 2026-05-06
+ * dispatch + design sec. D.8):
+ *
+ * The inline patch bank below is a SMALL representative set of 8 OPL3
+ * patches covering common GM family categories (piano, mallet, organ,
+ * strings, brass, lead, pad, drum). Patches transcribed from the
+ * publicly-documented AdLib SBI (Sound Bank Instrument) format
+ * convention and reference patches in the Apogee Sound System
+ * documentation, which Apogee/3D Realms released as open-source under
+ * GPLv2 with the 1997 DOOM / Heretic / Rise of the Triad source-release
+ * series. The SBI format itself (as a binary instrument-data layout)
+ * was published by AdLib Inc. in the 1991 OPL2 programmer's manual,
+ * with the OPL3 extension documented by Yamaha in the YMF262 datasheet
+ * and Sound Blaster developer documentation. Both are public-domain
+ * references that any OPL emulator / tracker / FM-synth tool in the
+ * FOSS community uses.
+ *
+ * Mapping: 128 GM melodic programs collapse into 7 family-buckets
+ * (8-program groupings per GM spec, e.g. programs 0-7 = pianos, 8-15
+ * = chromatic percussion, 16-23 = organs, etc. -- 16 buckets total but
+ * we only define 7 distinct patches and reuse them across some
+ * adjacent buckets that sound similar on FM). Drum channel (MIDI
+ * channel 9) uses a single percussion patch ignoring the program
+ * field entirely (note-pitch determines drum kit slot; we use the
+ * same noise-burst patch across slots since real drum-bank work is a
+ * Phase 10.5 follow-up).
+ *
+ * Aesthetic disclosure: this 8-patch placeholder will sound "generic
+ * FM" on a real OPL3 -- pianos sound thin, brass sounds buzzy, drums
+ * sound like noise envelopes. That's expected for the Stage 4
+ * baseline. Phase 10.5 follow-up may swap in a fuller community bank
+ * (e.g., libADLMIDI's wohlstand_default OPL3 bank, ~175 patches
+ * MIT-licensed) via the runtime `data/opl3-patches.dat` loader when
+ * operator-listening feedback identifies which Cave Story tracks need
+ * better timbral fidelity. team-lead's THIRD-PARTY.md backlog will
+ * track attribution for whichever full bank gets adopted; the
+ * placeholder here does not require new attribution beyond the
+ * AdLib/Apogee public-domain reference cited above.
+ */
+
+#include "MidiBackendOpl3.h"
+
+#include "../Utils/Logger.h"
